@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-time`

-- ca-interpretation-calendar.l4
--
-- The Interpretation Act (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. I-21: the time words of section 35(1) that need more than arithmetic,
-- and section 29.
-- Imports the time module (for `A moment` and `Coming into force`), `prelude` and `daydate`.
--
-- THE HOLIDAY LIST OF SECTION 35(1) IS PARTLY DATED BY THE TEXT AND PARTLY NOT.
--   Dated by the text:    Sunday; the first Monday in September, designated Labour Day; National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, observed on September 30.
--   Named, NOT dated by the text: New Year's Day, Good Friday, Easter Monday, Christmas Day, the birthday of the reigning Sovereign or
--   the day fixed by proclamation for it, Victoria Day, Canada Day, Remembrance Day, and every day appointed by proclamation or
--   by a provincial or municipal authority.
-- The first group is written here as three small tests.  The second group is an INPUT: the caller supplies a test for the days that
-- are holidays where the thing is to be done, and the Act's own three are added to it.  No calendar is written here.

§ `Section 35(1) "holiday": the days the text itself dates`

-- src:309 | holiday means any of the following days, namely, Sunday; New Year’s Day; Good Friday; Easter Monday; Christmas Day; the birthday or the day fixed by proclamation for the celebration of the birthday of the reigning Sovereign; Victoria Day; Canada Day; the first Monday in September, designated Labour Day; National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, which is observed on September 30; Remembrance Day; any day appointed by proclamation to be observed as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving; and any of the following additional days, namely,
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "holiday" (src:309)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a Sunday` d MEANS
    `Weekday of` d EQUALS Sunday

-- "the first Monday in September, designated Labour Day": a Monday in September whose number is at most seven.
-- src:309 | holiday means any of the following days, namely, Sunday; New Year’s Day; Good Friday; Easter Monday; Christmas Day; the birthday or the day fixed by proclamation for the celebration of the birthday of the reigning Sovereign; Victoria Day; Canada Day; the first Monday in September, designated Labour Day; National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, which is observed on September 30; Remembrance Day; any day appointed by proclamation to be observed as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving; and any of the following additional days, namely,
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "holiday" (src:309)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is Labour Day` d MEANS
        DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 9
    AND `Weekday of` d EQUALS Monday
    AND DATE_DAY d AT MOST 7

-- src:309 | holiday means any of the following days, namely, Sunday; New Year’s Day; Good Friday; Easter Monday; Christmas Day; the birthday or the day fixed by proclamation for the celebration of the birthday of the reigning Sovereign; Victoria Day; Canada Day; the first Monday in September, designated Labour Day; National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, which is observed on September 30; Remembrance Day; any day appointed by proclamation to be observed as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving; and any of the following additional days, namely,
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "holiday" (src:309)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation` d MEANS
        DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 9
    AND DATE_DAY d EQUALS 30

-- The list is a list of days "namely", so a day on it is a holiday and a day off it is not a holiday unless it is one of the
-- additional days: Saturday is not a holiday, and neither is the day before a holiday.
-- src:309 | holiday means any of the following days, namely, Sunday; New Year’s Day; Good Friday; Easter Monday; Christmas Day; the birthday or the day fixed by proclamation for the celebration of the birthday of the reigning Sovereign; Victoria Day; Canada Day; the first Monday in September, designated Labour Day; National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, which is observed on September 30; Remembrance Day; any day appointed by proclamation to be observed as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving; and any of the following additional days, namely,
-- src:310 | (a) in any province, any day appointed by proclamation of the lieutenant governor of the province to be observed as a public holiday or as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving within the province, and any day that is a non-juridical day by virtue of an Act of the legislature of the province, and
-- src:311 | (b) in any city, town, municipality or other organized district, any day appointed to be observed as a civic holiday by resolution of the council or other authority charged with the administration of the civic or municipal affairs of the city, town, municipality or district; (jour férié)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "holiday" (src:309-311)
GIVEN `the other holidays` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a holiday under section 35(1), given the other holidays` `the other holidays` d MEANS
        `is a Sunday` d
     OR `is Labour Day` d
     OR `is the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation` d
     OR `the other holidays` d

-- The same test as a function, which is the shape the time module takes: `FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN`.
-- src:309 | holiday means any of the following days, namely, Sunday; New Year’s Day; Good Friday; Easter Monday; Christmas Day; the birthday or the day fixed by proclamation for the celebration of the birthday of the reigning Sovereign; Victoria Day; Canada Day; the first Monday in September, designated Labour Day; National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, which is observed on September 30; Remembrance Day; any day appointed by proclamation to be observed as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving; and any of the following additional days, namely,
-- src:310 | (a) in any province, any day appointed by proclamation of the lieutenant governor of the province to be observed as a public holiday or as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving within the province, and any day that is a non-juridical day by virtue of an Act of the legislature of the province, and
-- src:311 | (b) in any city, town, municipality or other organized district, any day appointed to be observed as a civic holiday by resolution of the council or other authority charged with the administration of the civic or municipal affairs of the city, town, municipality or district; (jour férié)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "holiday" (src:309-311)
GIVEN `the other holidays` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
`the holiday test of section 35(1), given the other holidays` `the other holidays` MEANS
    GIVEN d YIELD `is a holiday under section 35(1), given the other holidays` `the other holidays` d

-- No other holidays: the caller has none to add, which the Act's three dated days still leave as a holiday calendar.
-- (Not the same as "no holidays": the other days the text names are not dated, so this test UNDER-reports.)
-- src:309 | holiday means any of the following days, namely, Sunday; New Year’s Day; Good Friday; Easter Monday; Christmas Day; the birthday or the day fixed by proclamation for the celebration of the birthday of the reigning Sovereign; Victoria Day; Canada Day; the first Monday in September, designated Labour Day; National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, which is observed on September 30; Remembrance Day; any day appointed by proclamation to be observed as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving; and any of the following additional days, namely,
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "holiday" (src:309)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no other holidays` d MEANS
    FALSE

-- Section 26, with the Act's own dated holidays and the caller's other holidays.
-- src:215 | 26 Where the time limited for the doing of a thing expires or falls on a holiday, the thing may be done on the day next following that is not a holiday.
-- src:309 | holiday means any of the following days, namely, Sunday; New Year’s Day; Good Friday; Easter Monday; Christmas Day; the birthday or the day fixed by proclamation for the celebration of the birthday of the reigning Sovereign; Victoria Day; Canada Day; the first Monday in September, designated Labour Day; National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, which is observed on September 30; Remembrance Day; any day appointed by proclamation to be observed as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving; and any of the following additional days, namely,
-- src:310 | (a) in any province, any day appointed by proclamation of the lieutenant governor of the province to be observed as a public holiday or as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving within the province, and any day that is a non-juridical day by virtue of an Act of the legislature of the province, and
-- src:311 | (b) in any city, town, municipality or other organized district, any day appointed to be observed as a civic holiday by resolution of the council or other authority charged with the administration of the civic or municipal affairs of the city, town, municipality or district; (jour férié)
@ref Interpretation Act s 26 (src:215) and s 35(1) "holiday" (src:309-311)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the other holidays` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for a thing under the Act's own dated holidays when the time limited ends on` d `given the other holidays` `the other holidays` MEANS
    `the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` d `given the holidays` (`the holiday test of section 35(1), given the other holidays` `the other holidays`)

§ `Section 35(1) "commencement"`

-- "commencement, when used with reference to an enactment, means the time at which the enactment comes into force".
-- The time is a moment (see the time module), and it exists only once a day is fixed.
-- src:283 | commencement, when used with reference to an enactment, means the time at which the enactment comes into force; (Version anglaise seulement)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "commencement" (src:283)
GIVEN c IS A `Coming into force`
GIVETH A `A moment`
`the commencement of an enactment that comes into force as` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `in force from` m THEN m
    WHEN `there is as yet no day from which it binds` THEN `no day yet decides the coming into force`

§ `Section 29 and section 35(1) "standard time"`

-- The seven standard times of the definition, with the hours behind Greenwich time that each paragraph gives.
DECLARE `A standard time` IS ONE OF
    `Newfoundland standard time`
    `Atlantic standard time`
    `eastern standard time`
    `central standard time`
    `mountain standard time`
    `Pacific standard time`
    `Yukon standard time`

-- src:336 | (a) in relation to the Province of Newfoundland and Labrador, Newfoundland standard time, being three hours and thirty minutes behind Greenwich time,
-- src:337 | (b) in relation to the Provinces of Nova Scotia, New Brunswick and Prince Edward Island, that part of the Province of Quebec lying east of the sixty-third meridian of west longitude, and that part of Nunavut lying east of the sixty-eighth meridian of west longitude, Atlantic standard time, being four hours behind Greenwich time,
-- src:338 | (c) in relation to that part of the Province of Quebec lying west of the sixty-third meridian of west longitude, that part of the Province of Ontario lying between the sixty-eighth and the ninetieth meridians of west longitude, Southampton Island and the islands adjacent to Southampton Island, and that part of Nunavut lying between the sixty-eighth and the eighty-fifth meridians of west longitude, eastern standard time, being five hours behind Greenwich time,
-- src:339 | (d) in relation to that part of the Province of Ontario lying west of the ninetieth meridian of west longitude, the Province of Manitoba, and that part of Nunavut, except Southampton Island and the islands adjacent to Southampton Island, lying between the eighty-fifth and the one hundred and second meridians of west longitude, central standard time, being six hours behind Greenwich time,
-- src:340 | (e) in relation to the Provinces of Saskatchewan and Alberta, the Northwest Territories and that part of Nunavut lying west of the one hundred and second meridian of west longitude, mountain standard time, being seven hours behind Greenwich time,
-- src:341 | (f) in relation to the Province of British Columbia, Pacific standard time, being eight hours behind Greenwich time, and
-- src:342 | (g) in relation to Yukon, Yukon standard time, being nine hours behind Greenwich time; (heure normale)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "standard time" (src:336-342)
GIVEN t IS A `A standard time`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minutes behind Greenwich time of` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `Newfoundland standard time` THEN 210
    WHEN `Atlantic standard time`     THEN 240
    WHEN `eastern standard time`      THEN 300
    WHEN `central standard time`      THEN 360
    WHEN `mountain standard time`     THEN 420
    WHEN `Pacific standard time`      THEN 480
    WHEN `Yukon standard time`        THEN 540

-- The places the definition names.  Three are cut by meridians of west longitude, which the caller supplies for the place in question.
DECLARE `A place the definition of standard time names` IS ONE OF
    `the Province of Newfoundland and Labrador`
    `the Province of Nova Scotia`
    `the Province of New Brunswick`
    `the Province of Prince Edward Island`
    `the Province of Quebec`
        HAS `degrees of west longitude of the place` IS A NUMBER
    `the Province of Ontario`
        HAS `degrees of west longitude of the place` IS A NUMBER
    `the Province of Manitoba`
    `the Province of Saskatchewan`
    `the Province of Alberta`
    `the Northwest Territories`
    `Nunavut`
        HAS `degrees of west longitude of the place` IS A NUMBER
    `Southampton Island or an island adjacent to Southampton Island`
    `the Province of British Columbia`
    `Yukon`

-- The standard time of a place, "except as otherwise provided by any proclamation of the Governor in Council that may be issued
-- for the purposes of this definition": the caller says whether such a proclamation provides one, and it wins if so.
-- A place exactly ON a meridian the definition names as a boundary is not answered: the text says "east of", "west of" and "between"
-- and does not say on which side a boundary line falls.
-- src:335 | standard time, except as otherwise provided by any proclamation of the Governor in Council that may be issued for the purposes of this definition in relation to any province or territory or any part thereof, means
-- src:336 | (a) in relation to the Province of Newfoundland and Labrador, Newfoundland standard time, being three hours and thirty minutes behind Greenwich time,
-- src:337 | (b) in relation to the Provinces of Nova Scotia, New Brunswick and Prince Edward Island, that part of the Province of Quebec lying east of the sixty-third meridian of west longitude, and that part of Nunavut lying east of the sixty-eighth meridian of west longitude, Atlantic standard time, being four hours behind Greenwich time,
-- src:338 | (c) in relation to that part of the Province of Quebec lying west of the sixty-third meridian of west longitude, that part of the Province of Ontario lying between the sixty-eighth and the ninetieth meridians of west longitude, Southampton Island and the islands adjacent to Southampton Island, and that part of Nunavut lying between the sixty-eighth and the eighty-fifth meridians of west longitude, eastern standard time, being five hours behind Greenwich time,
-- src:339 | (d) in relation to that part of the Province of Ontario lying west of the ninetieth meridian of west longitude, the Province of Manitoba, and that part of Nunavut, except Southampton Island and the islands adjacent to Southampton Island, lying between the eighty-fifth and the one hundred and second meridians of west longitude, central standard time, being six hours behind Greenwich time,
-- src:340 | (e) in relation to the Provinces of Saskatchewan and Alberta, the Northwest Territories and that part of Nunavut lying west of the one hundred and second meridian of west longitude, mountain standard time, being seven hours behind Greenwich time,
-- src:341 | (f) in relation to the Province of British Columbia, Pacific standard time, being eight hours behind Greenwich time, and
-- src:342 | (g) in relation to Yukon, Yukon standard time, being nine hours behind Greenwich time; (heure normale)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "standard time" (src:335-342)
GIVEN p IS A `A place the definition of standard time names`
      `a proclamation provides otherwise` IS A MAYBE `A standard time`
GIVETH A `A standard time`
`the standard time of` p `unless` `a proclamation provides otherwise` MEANS
    CONSIDER `a proclamation provides otherwise`
    WHEN JUST proclaimed THEN proclaimed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER p
        WHEN `the Province of Newfoundland and Labrador`                          THEN `Newfoundland standard time`
        WHEN `the Province of Nova Scotia`                                       THEN `Atlantic standard time`
        WHEN `the Province of New Brunswick`                                     THEN `Atlantic standard time`
        WHEN `the Province of Prince Edward Island`                              THEN `Atlantic standard time`
        WHEN `the Province of Quebec` w THEN
            IF   w EQUALS 63
            THEN `the text does not say on which side of a boundary meridian the line itself falls`
            ELSE IF w LESS THAN 63 THEN `Atlantic standard time` ELSE `eastern standard time`
        WHEN `the Province of Ontario` w THEN
            IF   w EQUALS 68 OR w EQUALS 90
            THEN `the text does not say on which side of a boundary meridian the line itself falls`
            ELSE IF   w LESS THAN 68
                 THEN `the text gives no standard time for the part of Ontario east of the sixty-eighth meridian`
                 ELSE IF w LESS THAN 90 THEN `eastern standard time` ELSE `central standard time`
        WHEN `the Province of Manitoba`                                          THEN `central standard time`
        WHEN `the Province of Saskatchewan`                                      THEN `mountain standard time`
        WHEN `the Province of Alberta`                                           THEN `mountain standard time`
        WHEN `the Northwest Territories`                                         THEN `mountain standard time`
        WHEN `Nunavut` w THEN
            IF   w EQUALS 68 OR w EQUALS 85 OR w EQUALS 102
            THEN `the text does not say on which side of a boundary meridian the line itself falls`
            ELSE IF   w LESS THAN 68
                 THEN `Atlantic standard time`
                 ELSE IF   w LESS THAN 85
                      THEN `eastern standard time`
                      ELSE IF   w LESS THAN 102
                           THEN `central standard time`
                           ELSE `mountain standard time`
        WHEN `Southampton Island or an island adjacent to Southampton Island`    THEN `eastern standard time`
        WHEN `the Province of British Columbia`                                  THEN `Pacific standard time`
        WHEN `Yukon`                                                             THEN `Yukon standard time`

-- src:335 | standard time, except as otherwise provided by any proclamation of the Governor in Council that may be issued for the purposes of this definition in relation to any province or territory or any part thereof, means
-- src:336 | (a) in relation to the Province of Newfoundland and Labrador, Newfoundland standard time, being three hours and thirty minutes behind Greenwich time,
-- src:337 | (b) in relation to the Provinces of Nova Scotia, New Brunswick and Prince Edward Island, that part of the Province of Quebec lying east of the sixty-third meridian of west longitude, and that part of Nunavut lying east of the sixty-eighth meridian of west longitude, Atlantic standard time, being four hours behind Greenwich time,
-- src:338 | (c) in relation to that part of the Province of Quebec lying west of the sixty-third meridian of west longitude, that part of the Province of Ontario lying between the sixty-eighth and the ninetieth meridians of west longitude, Southampton Island and the islands adjacent to Southampton Island, and that part of Nunavut lying between the sixty-eighth and the eighty-fifth meridians of west longitude, eastern standard time, being five hours behind Greenwich time,
-- src:339 | (d) in relation to that part of the Province of Ontario lying west of the ninetieth meridian of west longitude, the Province of Manitoba, and that part of Nunavut, except Southampton Island and the islands adjacent to Southampton Island, lying between the eighty-fifth and the one hundred and second meridians of west longitude, central standard time, being six hours behind Greenwich time,
-- src:340 | (e) in relation to the Provinces of Saskatchewan and Alberta, the Northwest Territories and that part of Nunavut lying west of the one hundred and second meridian of west longitude, mountain standard time, being seven hours behind Greenwich time,
-- src:341 | (f) in relation to the Province of British Columbia, Pacific standard time, being eight hours behind Greenwich time, and
-- src:342 | (g) in relation to Yukon, Yukon standard time, being nine hours behind Greenwich time; (heure normale)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "standard time" (src:335-342): a boundary meridian is not allotted to either side
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not say on which side of a boundary meridian the line itself falls` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text does not say on which side of a boundary meridian the line itself falls"

-- src:338 | (c) in relation to that part of the Province of Quebec lying west of the sixty-third meridian of west longitude, that part of the Province of Ontario lying between the sixty-eighth and the ninetieth meridians of west longitude, Southampton Island and the islands adjacent to Southampton Island, and that part of Nunavut lying between the sixty-eighth and the eighty-fifth meridians of west longitude, eastern standard time, being five hours behind Greenwich time,
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "standard time" (src:338): paragraph (c) starts at the sixty-eighth meridian
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text gives no standard time for the part of Ontario east of the sixty-eighth meridian` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text gives no standard time for the part of Ontario east of the sixty-eighth meridian"

-- A specified time of the day, in minutes after midnight, taken as standard time of the place (s 29), expressed as Greenwich time:
-- the minutes after Greenwich midnight of the same calendar day as the specified time, or after midnight of a later day if the sum passes a day.
DECLARE `A Greenwich time` HAS
    `whole days after the day specified` IS A NUMBER
    `minutes after Greenwich midnight`   IS A NUMBER

-- src:232 | 29 Where there is a reference to time expressed as a specified time of the day, the time is taken to mean standard time.
-- src:335 | standard time, except as otherwise provided by any proclamation of the Governor in Council that may be issued for the purposes of this definition in relation to any province or territory or any part thereof, means
@ref Interpretation Act s 29 (src:232) and s 35(1) "standard time" (src:335)
GIVEN `the minutes after midnight specified` IS A NUMBER
      p IS A `A place the definition of standard time names`
      `a proclamation provides otherwise` IS A MAYBE `A standard time`
GIVETH A `A Greenwich time`
`the Greenwich time of a time of the day of` `the minutes after midnight specified` `at` p `unless` `a proclamation provides otherwise` MEANS
    IF       `the minutes after midnight specified` AT LEAST 0
         AND `the minutes after midnight specified` LESS THAN 1440
         AND FLOOR `the minutes after midnight specified` EQUALS `the minutes after midnight specified`
    THEN `A Greenwich time`
             WITH `whole days after the day specified` IS FLOOR (total DIVIDED BY 1440)
                  `minutes after Greenwich midnight`   IS total MODULO 1440
    ELSE `the Act has no rule for a time of the day that is not a whole number of minutes from 0 to 1439`
    WHERE
        total MEANS `the minutes after midnight specified` PLUS `the minutes behind Greenwich time of` (`the standard time of` p `unless` `a proclamation provides otherwise`)

-- src:232 | 29 Where there is a reference to time expressed as a specified time of the day, the time is taken to mean standard time.
@ref Interpretation Act s 29 (src:232)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Act has no rule for a time of the day that is not a whole number of minutes from 0 to 1439` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Act has no rule for a time of the day that is not a whole number of minutes from 0 to 1439"

-- "local time": "the time observed in that place for the regulation of business hours".  What that is, is a fact about a place
-- that the Act does not state.
-- src:323 | local time, in relation to any place, means the time observed in that place for the regulation of business hours; (heure locale)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "local time" (src:323)
GIVEN p IS A `A place the definition of standard time names`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minutes behind Greenwich time of the local time of` p MEANS
    REFUSE "the Act does not say what time a place observes for the regulation of business hours"
